# Stripe Integration Guide — Crave Bakery
# Learning Mode — Using stripe/stripe-php (Raw SDK)

> **Purpose:** This file guides you through integrating Stripe payments into the Crave Bakery project
> using the raw `stripe/stripe-php` SDK for learning purposes.
>
> **⚠️ Learning Note:** This integration uses `stripe/stripe-php` to follow along with instructor videos.
> When the project goes live, this will be replaced with `laravel/cashier`.
> The Stripe concepts (PaymentIntent, Webhooks, test cards) are identical — only the code style changes.
>
> Load alongside: `crave-bakery-project-brief.md` and `cursor-learning-rules.md`

---

## The Plan — Learning Now vs Going Live Later

```
NOW (Learning)                        LATER (Production)
──────────────────────────────────    ──────────────────────────────────
stripe/stripe-php (raw SDK)     →     laravel/cashier (Laravel wrapper)
Manual Stripe::setApiKey()      →     Cashier handles automatically
Manual PaymentIntent::create()  →     $user->createPaymentIntent()
Manual webhook verification     →     Cashier built-in WebhookController
```

**Everything you learn now transfers directly** — same Stripe Dashboard, same test cards,
same API keys, same concepts. Only the PHP code style changes when going live.

---

## Before You Start — Test Mode Explained

```
Stripe has two modes:
  Test Mode  → fake money, fake cards, safe to experiment ✅  ← WE ARE HERE
  Live Mode  → real money, real cards, needs business account

We are ALWAYS in Test Mode during learning.
You can tell by the orange "TEST MODE" banner in the Stripe dashboard.
```

**Test card numbers you will use:**
```
Successful payment:     4242 4242 4242 4242
Card declined:          4000 0000 0000 0002
Requires 3D Secure:     4000 0025 0000 3155
Insufficient funds:     4000 0000 0000 9995
Expiry:  any future date (e.g. 12/29)
CVC:     any 3 digits   (e.g. 123)
ZIP:     any 5 digits   (e.g. 10001)
```

---

## What We Are Building

```
Customer fills checkout form
         ↓
Clicks "Place Order"
         ↓
Our Laravel backend creates a Stripe PaymentIntent
         ↓
Vue frontend uses Stripe.js to collect card details securely
         ↓
Stripe processes the payment
         ↓
Webhook hits our server to confirm payment succeeded
         ↓
Order status updates to "paid" + "processing"
         ↓
Customer sees confirmation page
```

